WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
Welcome to Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 93 for June 6th, 2026.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.860
The universe has been busy, let's get into it.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:13.040
Astronomers have finally detected winds streaming from the Milky Way's central black hole

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:20.140
after a 50-year search. After 50 years of searching, astronomers identified powerful winds flowing

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:26.660
outward from Sagittarius A screen. The winds appear as a cone-shaped cavity in surrounding gas

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:32.700
and dust. Observations used multiple telescopes to map the empty region pointing back to the

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:38.780
black hole. The discovery confirms theoretical predictions that active black holes drive galactic

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:44.860
scale outflows. Further mapping will reveal how these winds affect star formation in the galactic

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:51.140
center. Now, here's something that blew my mind when I looked into it. Astronomers have now mapped

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:57.520
winds streaming from Sagittarius A to Esk after decades of effort. The cone-shaped cavity in

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:03.040
surrounding material points directly back to the black hole and matches long-standing predictions

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:09.720
for active galactic nuclei. Multiteloscope data revealed the empty region carved by outflowing gas.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:16.640
The finding strengthens models of how central black holes regulate star formation across entire galaxies.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:22.280
How far do these winds extend and do they influence the Milky Way's overall evolution?

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:29.980
If the Sun were scaled to the size of a basketball in Toronto, Sagittarius A2 would still be smaller

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:36.820
than a single atom yet contained four million times the Sun's mass. Material spiraling inward

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:42.300
releases enormous energy that heats and accelerates surrounding gas into powerful outflows.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:48.440
These winds can reach thousands of kilometers per second and clear cavities hundreds of light

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:54.700
years across. The process links the tiny region near the event horizon to structures visible across

00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:01.040
the entire galaxy. We can measure the wind speed and extent, yet the exact fraction of energy

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:07.500
converted into outflow versus radiation remains unknown. The European Space Agency set the next

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:15.360
Ariane 6 launch for June 17 in its most powerful configuration to date. Flight VA269 will carry 36

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:21.460
satellites for Amazon's project Kuiper constellation. The rocket's upgraded boosters will deliver

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:27.760
greater payload capacity than earlier flights. Engineers completed final checks on the vehicle and ground

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:33.260
systems ahead of the window. The mission will test the launcher's performance with a large commercial

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:39.760
manifest. On a completely different node, NASA completed a test showing a spacecraft can move

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:45.460
between multiple satellite communication networks without losing contact. The demonstration used

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:50.780
existing ground stations and commercial relay satellites to maintain continuous links.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.860
Engineers tracked signal handoffs during orbital passes to confirm reliability.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:00.780
The result supports future missions that may need flexible communication paths.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:05.900
Additional tests are planned to refine switching protocols for longer duration flights.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:11.420
The International Academy of Astronautics SETI committee revised its declaration of principles

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:17.920
for handling potential detections of extraterrestrial intelligence. The updates address how findings should

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:23.660
be verified and shared publicly. The changes coincide with the upcoming release of the film

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:29.440
Disclosure Day. Committee members reviewed decades-old procedures to reflect current detection

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:35.320
capabilities. The revised document will guide future announcements if signals are confirmed.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:41.980
A total solar eclipse will cross a remote region of Northern Russia on August 12, 2026.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:47.940
The moon's shadow will produce totality for observers along a narrow path during midday.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:54.920
Partial phases will be visible across Greenland and Iceland. NASA released maps showing the exact

00:03:54.920 --> 00:04:00.440
track and timing for the event. The eclipse offers a rare opportunity for ground-based

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:06.160
coronal studies. Two of the three small sats for NASA's Incuse mission finished assembly and

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:11.940
environmental testing. The mission will study tropical convective storm dynamics from orbit starting

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:18.600
in 2027. The third satellite remains in testing with completion expected no earlier than September.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:24.600
Incuse will provide the first space-based survey of updraft behavior inside storms.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.540
Data will improve weather and climate models. Good year will supply tires for NASA's

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:36.820
Artemis moon rover missions. The tires must operate in the moon's extreme temperatures and abrasive

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:43.920
regolith. Development builds on earlier testing of non-numatic wheel concepts. The contract supports

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:50.280
surface mobility needs for sustained lunar operations. Prototypes will undergo further evaluation

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:57.640
before flight hardware production. NASA's X-59 Experimental Aircraft reached Mach 1.1 during

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:03.840
a June 5th test flight from Edwards Air Force Base. The 81-minute flight focused on handling

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:10.140
qualities at both subsonic and supersonic speeds. Test pilot Jim Clueless flew the aircraft

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:17.980
to 43,400 feet. The milestone advances plans for quiet supersonic demonstrations later this year.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.420
Data from the flight will help validate the aircraft's low-boom design.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:29.380
The Hubble Space Telescope captured M88, a spiral galaxy traveling through the Virgo cluster on a

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:35.100
journey expected to last hundreds of millions of years. The image shows the galaxy's arms and

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:41.080
central bulge as it moves toward the cluster's dense center. Hubble's observations track how

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:47.600
cluster environments reshape galaxies over long time scales. The data add to ongoing studies of

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:53.920
galaxy evolution within dense cosmic neighborhoods. Future observations with larger telescopes will

00:05:53.920 --> 00:06:00.360
measure changes in M88 structure as it continues inward. Researchers at the University of California

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:06.180
Riverside used James Webb Space Telescope data to trace the cosmic web back to when the universe

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:12.700
was 1 billion years old. The map shows the network of galaxies and gas filaments in unprecedented

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:18.880
detail. Earlier surveys lacked the sensitivity to resolve structures at such early epochs.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:25.400
The new view helps test models of how the first galaxies assembled. Additional JWST

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:32.320
fields will extend the map to even earlier times. Astronomers at CNRS and the University of Bordeaux

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:38.240
directly observe the rotation of a proto-planetary disk around the young star, AB-Origay.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:44.080
The disk shows clear velocity patterns consistent with material orbiting the central star.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:50.660
This marks one of the first live kinematic maps of such a system. The observations help

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:56.980
refine models of how planets form within rotating disks. Follow-up studies will track changes in

00:06:56.980 --> 00:07:03.420
disk structure over time. A new study of a binary star pair reveals dramatically different chemical

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:10.200
compositions, despite likely forming together. One star displays abundance patterns suggesting its

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:17.360
swallowed planets or planetesimals. The research, posted to archive on May 29, offers a possible

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:23.600
solution to the observed chemical mismatch. High resolution spectra provided the elemental data

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:30.120
used in the analysis. Additional observations of similar systems may show how often such events occur.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:36.260
The Zvezda Service Module Transfer Tunnel continues to show small atmosphere leaks first

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:43.160
noted in 2019. Ross Cosmos has applied temporary and permanent sealants while monitoring the

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:49.720
rate of loss. NASA and Ross Cosmos teams identified the root cause through joint analysis.

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:54.960
Crew operations remain normal outside of brief precautionary shelter periods.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:08:01.060
Further mitigation steps are under review. Next time, keep an eye on final vehicle checks

